Adaptation: Go test-only restatement, in
internal/agent/sampling_truncation_invariants_test.go, of the upstream
top-p/top-k boundary checks (no pruned token outranks a survivor, survivors
keep their probabilities, the kept prefix is minimal and reaches the top-p or
top-k boundary) for fak's semantics: top-k first, then top-p over the
post-top-k mass with an inclusive stop. The checks use exact float64
comparisons in fak's stable descending summation order instead of the
upstream eps. A short reference of the upstream rule (top-p over the full
distribution with a strict exclusive-mass stop, then stable top-k) is used
only to pin the CD-02 composition and CD-03 boundary-equality divergence rows.
No upstream source is copied, nothing serving-side calls the test, and the
production sampler is unchanged.
